WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.433
How can light
reveal an obstacle

2
00:00:02.433 --> 00:00:03.667
without being absorbed

3
00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.300
or reflected by it?

4
00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.233
Start with one photon

5
00:00:07.233 --> 00:00:08.767
and two possible paths

6
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:09.933
that meet again.

7
00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.333
In this carefully
aligned setup,

8
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:14.900
the waves associated
with the paths

9
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.633
cancel at one output.

10
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:18.367
This detector stays dark.

11
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.133
Now block one path

12
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.333
with an absorber.

13
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.000
Sometimes it absorbs
the photon.

14
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.467
That trial ends.

15
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.300
But in another trial,

16
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.933
the dark detector clicks.

17
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.833
The photon reached
this detector.

18
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.867
The obstacle was detected,

19
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.867
without absorbing
that photon.

20
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:36.533
Why?

21
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.400
Blocking one possible path

22
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.800
removed the cancellation

23
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.133
that kept this detector dark.

24
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.967
This is interaction-free
measurement,

25
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:46.933
demonstrated in experiments.

26
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.800
It succeeds only
in some trials.

27
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.467
Others absorb the photon,

28
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.567
or give no clear answer.
